        "score": null,
        "description": "<p style=\"margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:1em;margin-left:0px;padding:0px;line-height:1.4;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:14px;line-height:14.98px;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;\">Hello most lovely students, and the rest of you as well.&nbsp; I wish I could be here today but I am needed elsewhere.&nbsp; Our work on Antigone is going well and I am so excited by the work and thought you have shown.&nbsp; I think it would be most advantageous or us to&nbsp;<span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;\">not</span>&nbsp;put the set up but to work with your scene partner (s) and get your lines down solid.</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px;padding:0px;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:14px;line-height:14.98px;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;\">Chorus if you could meet and read through the rest of the script and try to divide the lines up amongst yourselves. Remember some of the chorus stays loyal to Creon and some shifts and starts to question and blame him. Let these chorus members stay consistent.</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px;padding:0px;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:14px;line-height:14.98px;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;\">I will see you again on Tuesday and I can’t wait to see where we are with this production.</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px;padding:0px;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:14px;line-height:14.98px;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px 0px;padding:0px;line-height:1.4;\"><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:14px;line-height:14.98px;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;\">Hobby</span></p>",
